.TH "BANDE" "1" "" "bande" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bande \- what the installed Bande programs can do
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bande
.RI [ domain
.RI [ verb
.RI [ arguments ...]]]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B bande undo
.RI [ receipt ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Carries out the intents of the installed programs, which it finds in
.IR /usr/share/bande/intents .
Without a verb it lists what can be done. A verb on something other than the domain's main noun is
written with a hyphen, as in
.BR "bande mail create\-draft" .
.PP
Required arguments follow in the order
.B \-\-help
shows; the others are given as
.BI \-\- name " value"
and may be repeated where a list is taken. Words that are left are the text to find.
.PP
.B bande undo
takes back the change of a receipt, or the newest one of all programs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the answer or the error as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show what a command takes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when it was done, else 1.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bande settings find "dark mode"
bande settings get appearance text\-size
bande settings set appearance light
bande undo
.fi
